  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response for Women&apos;s Protection in Gnagna Province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gagna has experienced a number of shocks since 2023, resulting in a significant deterioration of the humanitarian situation in the area. In May, Unidentified Armed Groups (UAGs) entered various rural villages in Gnagna province and ordered local populations to leave the area. As a result, a large number of IDPs fled to seek refuge in other areas within the province, focusing mainly on larger towns. Estimated number of IDPs in the area reached 54,153 by end of project. IRC is proposing a women and girls&apos; protection response, focused on WGSS, GBV case management, PSS, service mapping and safe referral services, distribution of dignity kits, security audits, awareness raising and risk mitigation around GBV and available services, and capacity building of local stakeholders and service providers on key GBV concepts and services.</narrative>
  </description>
